.TH hamurabi 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
hamurabi \- govern ancient Sumeria
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hamurabi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The old Hamurabi game, in Brian Troutwine's C.  You rule the city for a
ten-year term.  Each year your steward reports how many people starved
and how many arrived, any plague, the harvest, what the rats ate, the
grain in store and the price of land, and then asks four questions, each
answered with a number:
.IP 1. 4
how many acres of land to buy,
.IP 2. 4
how many to sell,
.IP 3. 4
how many bushels of grain to feed the people \- each needs 20 a year,
.IP 4. 4
how many acres to plant with seed.
.PP
Starve more than 45 per cent of the people in one year and you are
thrown out of office.  At the end of the term your rule is judged on the
people who starved and the land each citizen has left.
